s well as the military use of cavalry. The Oyo Empire was one of the most politically important states in Western Africa from the late-16th to the early 18th century and held sway not only over most of the other kingdoms in Yorubaland, but also over nearby African states, notably the Fon Kingdom of Dahomey in modern Benin to its west."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q849623","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q18342086","value_label":"Oyo-Ile","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Oyo-Ile"},{"qid":"Q849623","kind":"religion","value_qid":"Q1086440","value_label":"Yoruba religion","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P140","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Yoruba religion"}],"people":{},"media":{},"names":["Imperio oyo","Impero Oyo","Império Oyo","Império de Oyo","Koninkrijk Oyo","Königreich Oyo","Oió","Ojo","Oyo","Oyo Empire","Oyo İmparatorluğu","Oyo帝国","Oyó","Reino de Oyo","Reino de Oyo.","Royaume d’Oyo","royaume d'Oyo","Αυτοκρατορία Όγιο","Ойо","إمبراطورية الأويو","ओयो साम्राज्य","オヨ帝国","オヨ王国","オヨ＝イレ","奧約帝國"]}